{"title":"Minimum End Removals to Make a Palindrome","difficulty":"Medium","statement":"You are given a string `s`. In one operation you may remove a single character from the **left end** of the string or from the **right end** of the string. You may remove characters from the left only, from the right only, or from both ends, in any order and any number of times (including zero).\n\nReturn the **minimum number of characters** that must be removed so that the remaining string is a palindrome (it reads the same forwards and backwards).\n\nOnly characters at the two ends can be removed; you cannot delete characters from the middle. A single remaining character is always a palindrome, so an answer always exists.","inputFormat":"A single line containing the string `s`.","outputFormat":"Print one integer: the minimum number of removed characters.","constraints":["1 ≤ |s| ≤ 2000","`s` consists of lowercase English letters"],"examples":[{"input":"xabcbay","output":"2","explanation":"Removing `x` from the left and `y` from the right leaves `abcba`, a palindrome. No string with fewer removals is a palindrome."},{"input":"abcd","output":"3","explanation":"The longest palindrome that can be kept is a single character, so 3 characters are removed."},{"input":"racecar","output":"0","explanation":"The string is already a palindrome."}],"tests":[{"input":"a","output":"0"},{"input":"aa","output":"0"},{"input":"ab","output":"1"},{"input":"aba","output":"0"},{"input":"abba","output":"0"},{"input":"abc","output":"2"},{"input":"zzzzzzz","output":"0"},{"input":"abcdcbaxyz","output":"3"},{"input":"xyzabccba","output":"3"},{"input":"aab","output":"1"},{"input":"baa","output":"1"},{"input":"ccbabacbaaabcaaabacacccaa","output":"16"},{"input":"bbbababaaaababbabaaabaaa","output":"12"},{"input":"abbaabbaabbbb","output":"3"},{"input":"baaaacaaccccca","output":"7"},{"input":"aaaabbababbbbbabbbababbbaabb","output":"17"},{"input":"aabacabbbcbbabbacbb","output":"14"},{"input":"pztecgubggzklyrgb","